# Prompt specialization ratchet (R1188-U1: generalize, don't specialize).
#
# The ceiling on (source file, prompt) pairs where code under rust/src/ or js/
# holds verbatim, outside comments, a prompt that a test sends to Formal AI.
# Such a string is a branch, cue or canned answer keyed to one prompt; the
# general rule lives in seed data. scripts/check-prompt-specialization.mjs
# fails above the ceiling and asks for it to be lowered below it, so the
# number only falls.
#
# History. 23 pairs in .rs, .mjs and .js fell to 0 on 2026-10-08 (the
# behavior-rule catalog, the capability listings, the example prompts of the
# knowledge export and the offline translation phrases moved to seed data).
# The same day the scan widened to the browser app's .jsx files, which it had
# skipped, and found 17 pairs there (the sidebar example prompts of
# js/app/app-constants.jsx and the local fallbacks of js/app/local-*.jsx), so
# the ceiling was re-based to 17 from a wider measurement, not a regression.
prompt-specialization-ratchet
  specialization-ceiling 17
